Article 92 Whoever commits any of the following acts shall be ordered by the competent superior authority to return the intercepted or misappropriated funds within a time limit, and the illegal income shall be confiscated; and the person directly in charge and other persons directly responsible shall be given administrative sanctions by the competent superior authority or the unit to which they belong; if a crime is constituted, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law:
(1) Intercepting or misappropriating funds for grain purchase in violation of the provisions of Paragraph 3 of Article 33 of this Law;
(2) Intercepting or misappropriating fiscal funds and credit funds for agriculture in violation of the provisions of Paragraph 2 of Article 39 of this Law;
(3) Intercepting or misappropriating poverty alleviation funds in violation of the provisions of Paragraph 3 of Article 86 of this Law.

Article 94 Whoever commits any of the following acts shall be ordered by the competent superior authority to cease the illegal act, and the person directly in charge and other persons directly responsible shall be given administrative sanctions, and the illegally collected fund-raising money, taxes or fees shall be ordered to be returned:
(1) Conducting illegal fund-raising, standard-reaching, upgrading or acceptance-checking activities in rural areas, in violation of the provisions of Article 68 of this Law;
(2) Levying taxes on farmers by illegal methods, in violation of the provisions of Article 69 of this Law;
(3) Charging farmers beyond the prescribed amount or items through rural primary and secondary schools, in violation of the provisions of Article 70 of this Law.
